{'exec_id': 14, 'findings_note': 'The population-differentiated RT threshold, searched directly for the first time. Returns BOTH held OD-5 leads as hits 1 and 2: Iglehart REF-00578 (CI children, RT 0.3/0.6/0.9 s) and Iglehart REF-00325 (hearing-aid children, same design) - the project already owned the strongest Tier-1 evidence on its own flagship parameter and could not see it, because the R9 duplicate gate queries evidence_sources only and is blind to all 835 source_locators rows (OD-5). R15 NOTE, AND MY OWN ERROR CORRECTED IN THE SAME ROW: I first wrote here that the reasoning doc calling this one Iglehart 2020 was wrong and that the record said 2019. That was an INFERENCE FROM THE DOI STRING (10.1044/2019_AJA-19-0010) plus a result listing, not from a payload. The retrieved Crossref payload says issued 2020, volume 29, issue 1, pages 6-17 - the DOI slug carries the assignment year, not the publication year. THE REASONING DOC WAS RIGHT AND I WAS WRONG. Caught and corrected BEFORE any admission was written, so no bibliographic field inherited it. Same failure class as the batch this session audits: a bibliographic claim written from something other than the bytes. NOTE FOR D-0165: every population in this yield is deaf or hard-of-hearing children, and DEAF carries ZERO item_population_links on this slug, so the strongest evidence for the parameter serves a population the item layer does not connect to it.'}
